Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'delegation: using a feature and configuring the infrastructure for it are different permissions. org_admin was the whole guard on every sensitive surface, so holding it meant holding the customers Twilio account and the power to register their A2P brand - a brand binds permanently to the account that creates it, which is the one messaging mistake that cannot be cleanly undone. Splits one boolean into the three states the business actually has. FEATURE ENABLED stays enabled_features and says the customer may USE a service. SELF MANAGEMENT ALLOWED is a new delegated_capabilities column and says the ORGANIZATION may ADMINISTER the infrastructure behind it. ADMIN GRANT is a new user_capability_grants table and says THIS named administrator holds it. Restland is the worked example: sms enabled, nothing delegated, so advisors send all day and nobody there can see the Twilio account those messages go through. New capabilities service mirrors entitlements line for line rather than inventing a second authorization framework - one resolve() with a fixed order where every step can only deny, god bypassing both gates, and feature checked before role because your organization does not have sms is a truer answer than you are not an administrator. Membership was the obvious reuse and is the wrong shape: its column is role, its vocabulary is sales_manager and sales_rep, and sales_access reads it to decide who runs a sales team. A role is who you ARE, a capability is what you MAY DO. Role is now an eligibility filter only, so an advisor cannot receive an infrastructure capability even from a stray grant row, and set_user_grants refuses to write one. Platform wide capabilities are delegable=False and refused with a 400, so no screen can hand master billing to a customer however it is used. Closes the cross brand hole found in phase 1 first and proves it: PATCH /org-settings/features never called _resolve_org, so a super_admin on one brand could rewrite another brands customers entitlements, and it json.dumps()d whatever it was handed with no validation and no audit - which is how a2p_10dlc and master_dashboard got stored in a column whose registry had never contained them, and that was the unknown feature key warning. Both writers now share one set of rules. Consolidates three disagreeing feature vocabularies into one: seven orphan sidebar keys registered, OrgManagers own list deleted in favour of the servers, and a2p_10dlc removed from the feature vocabulary entirely and from the growth, professional and standard plan tiers - a plan can sell the SMS service, it cannot sell the carrier identity. Advisor Twilio credential write is gone rather than gated: it had no role check at all, and a capability nobody should hold is better deleted than delegated. billing/plans was public and served the whole price list to anyone, for a plan picker that does not exist. God control screen gets an administration tab separate from features, reporting all three states as three blocks with effective showing both gates applied, so a grant that is inert because the organization is not self managing says so rather than being inferred. System Health wording is brand neutral now; cadence behaviour is untouched and the scheduler was never the problem. Gate 27 adds 71 checks across all eleven proof cases; reverting to a role check produces 14 leaks including Restlands stored Account SID actually being overwritten. Three existing gates changed with justification, one of which was asserting billing/plans must be public.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
